# EIP install config — preprod (production rehearsal). No seeding; frontend is a production build
# served by vite preview; operators enter their tenant id in the UI.
#
# OIDC is now REQUIRED to boot (DEBT-012, M5 Wave S1a): ProductionTenantResolutionGuard refuses
# prod/preprod startup unless EIP_SECURITY_MODE=oidc and EIP_OIDC_ISSUER is a real (non-CHANGE_ME)
# issuer — the dev header resolver must never serve rehearsal-of-production traffic either. The
# CHANGE_ME placeholder below follows the DEBT-005 convention: the operator replaces it with their
# enterprise IdP realm (or the Compose dev Keycloak's http://localhost:8180/auth/realms/eip for a
# local rehearsal) before this environment will boot.
#
# Same DEBT-005 convention applies to the secrets below: ProductionSecretsGuard
# (com.eip.app.config) refuses prod/preprod boot while EIP_APP_DB_PASSWORD /
# EIP_MIGRATOR_DB_PASSWORD / EIP_SECRETS_MASTER_KEY / EIP_API_CURSOR_SIGNING_KEY are blank,
# CHANGE_ME, or a known dev/demo fixture value — a preprod rehearsal must exercise real secret
# provisioning, not silently inherit scripts/install/install.sh's hardcoded local dev DB password.
# An operator running a genuine preprod rehearsal (not via scripts/install/install.sh, which always
# injects the local dev DB password and does not set EIP_SECRETS_MASTER_KEY /
# EIP_API_CURSOR_SIGNING_KEY) must export real values for all four before this environment will
# boot; EIP_DB_URL / EIP_APP_DB_USER / EIP_MIGRATOR_DB_USER are left at their application.yaml
# defaults (local Compose Postgres) since usernames/URLs are not secret-bearing.
SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=preprod
VITE_MODE=preprod
FRONTEND_SERVE=preview      # preview = vite build --mode preprod + vite preview
COMPOSE_PROFILES=core,observability
EIP_BACKEND_PORT=8080
VITE_PORT=5173
SEEDED=0
EIP_APP_DB_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME
EIP_MIGRATOR_DB_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME
EIP_SECRETS_MASTER_KEY=CHANGE_ME
# Pagination-cursor HMAC signing key (DEBT-010, ApiCursorSigningProperties) — base64 of 32 bytes.
EIP_API_CURSOR_SIGNING_KEY=CHANGE_ME
EIP_SECURITY_MODE=oidc
EIP_OIDC_ISSUER=CHANGE_ME
